# NOT GENERATED. `make_helper_proxies.py` used to write this file, and used to
# write the `hair` proxy that wore it; neither is true any more -- the long hair
# is grown as cards by `tools/make_long_hair.py` and wears `hair_card.mhmat`.
#
# The file stays because a material is a USER-FACING CHOICE: the Materials tab
# lists these, and the 52-strand sheet is still a perfectly good look to put on
# a shell-like style. It is hand-maintained from here, which is worth saying
# plainly -- a banner naming a tool that no longer touches a file sends the next
# person to refresh it with the wrong generator.
#
# THE STRAND TEXTURE THIS SLOT SPENT ITS LIFE ASKING FOR.
#
# This comment used to read: "real hair needs an alpha-cut strand
# texture, which the cage geometry cannot stand in for". The second
# half was wrong about the reason. The geometry could carry one
# perfectly well; what it could not do was MAP one, because the four
# generated styles had no UVs at all -- measured on an export, body
# 14,517 distinct UVs, eyes 808, teeth 136, hair ZERO.
#
# The sweeps emit UVs now (u around the tube, v along it) and
# tools/make_hair_alpha.py writes the texture, so both halves exist.
#
# `transparent True` is load-bearing and not cosmetic: the eye
# material records that "without the flag the renderer discards that
# alpha and paints an opaque disc over the iris". Here it would
# paint a solid tube with a stripe pattern on it.
name Hair
tag MakeHuman™
ambientColor 0.04 0.03 0.02
diffuseColor 0.28 0.19 0.13
specularColor 0.6 0.6 0.6
shininess 0.3
opacity 1.0
transparent True
diffuseTexture ../hair_strands.png
backfaceCull True
castShadows True
receiveShadows True
shader data/shaders/glsl/litsphere
